    "question": "Ben has 8 apples more than Phillip does. Tom has three eighths as many apples at Ben has. If Phillip has 40 apples, how many apples does Tom have?",
    "gold": "18",
    "answer": "Ben has 40+8 = <<40+8=48>>48 apples.\nThere are 48/8 = <<48/8=6>>6 apples in every eighth.\nTom has 6*3 = <<6*3=18>>18 apples.\n#### 18"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many apples Tom has, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify how many apples Ben has.\n2. Use the number of apples Ben has to find out how many apples Tom has.\n\nFirst, we know that Phillip has 40 apples. According to the problem, Ben has 8 apples more than Phillip. Therefore, we can calculate the number of apples Ben has as follows:\n\\[\n\\text{Number of apples Ben has} = \\text{Number of apples Phillip has} + 8 = 40 + 8 = 48\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find out how many apples Tom has. The problem states that Tom has three eighths as many apples as Ben has. So, we calculate the number of apples Tom has as follows:\n\\[\n\\text{Number of apples Tom has} = \\frac{3}{8} \\times \\text{Number of apples Ben has} = \\frac{3}{8} \\times 48 = 18\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of apples Tom has is \\(\\boxed{18}\\).",
